TITLE:: SDGSync
summary:: long samples played together at one tempo and in one key, written as Tidal code
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SDGSyncWindow, Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGSampleTags

DESCRIPTION::
Works out how to play several longer samples together - drum loops, arpeggios, pads - at one
tempo, and in one key if they have one. It writes the Tidal code: code::setcps::, then a
code::d:: for each sample with code::loopAt::, code::chop:: and, where the key needs it, a
code::speed::. It reads each sample's bpm, first beat and key from link::Classes/SDGSampleTags::,
the analysis or what was set by hand.

code::
y = ~sdg.sync;
y.add(\breaks125, 0); y.add(\breaks152, 0);
y.bpm = 125;
y.plan.collect { |r| [r[\label], r[\cycles], r[\rate]] };
y.code.postln;
y.play;
y.stop;
::

A loop of code::b:: bpm that holds code::beats:: beats plays as code::loopAt (beats / beatsPerCycle)::,
which reads it at code::t / b:: of its speed: on the grid, and that much higher or lower in pitch.
A loop nearer half or twice the tempo is counted in half or double time. A loop that is not a whole
number of beats plays its whole beats only, with code::# end e # speed e::. With link::#-matchKey::, a
sample tagged code::melodic::, or with a key set by hand, gets a code::speed:: that takes it the rest
of the way into link::#-key::, less than a tritone either way; link::#-chopsPerBeat:: keeps it on the
grid. The page code::docs/sync.md:: of the repository explains why each of these is done.

It sends code::changed:: with code::\sync:: when a sample or a setting changes, and with
code::\playing:: when the preview starts or stops. One belongs to each link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::,
made by link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-sync::, stopped and closed by its code::free::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: sdg
a link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::. Use link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-sync:: rather than making another.

METHOD:: chopChoices
The pieces a beat the window offers, code::[0, 1, 2, 4, 8]::; 0 is no chop.

METHOD:: latency
The preview's events, all with this latency, so they line up. 0.2 s.

METHOD:: minOffset
A first beat later than this, in seconds, is shifted onto the grid with code::<~::. 0.015.

METHOD:: wholeTolerance
How far, in beats, a loop may be from a whole number before it is trimmed to its whole beats. 0.12.

METHOD:: isTonal
ARGUMENT:: info
what link::Classes/SDGSampleTags#-infoOf:: answers for a sample.
RETURNS:: whether its pitch is matched: it has a key or a note, and is tagged code::melodic:: or had its key set by hand.

METHOD:: wantedTonic
ARGUMENT:: mode
the sample's: code::\major::, code::\minor:: or code::\note::.
ARGUMENT:: target
code::(tonic:, mode:)::.
RETURNS:: the tonic the sample goes to: a note to the target's tonic, a minor sample into a major key to its relative minor, a major one into a minor key to its relative major.

METHOD:: keyName
ARGUMENT:: tonic
0 .. 11.
ARGUMENT:: mode
ARGUMENT:: given
a note's own name, kept for a note.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/String:: such as code::"C#m"::.

METHOD:: num
ARGUMENT:: x
ARGUMENT:: decimals
RETURNS:: x as Tidal code, rounded, with no trailing zeros.

METHOD:: signed
ARGUMENT:: x
ARGUMENT:: decimals
RETURNS:: x with its sign, for semitones.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: sdg
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.

METHOD:: items
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/List:: of code::(bank:, index:)::, in the order of the code.

METHOD:: add
ARGUMENT:: bank
ARGUMENT:: index
Adds a sample of the library and puts it first in the analysis queue.
RETURNS:: its place, or nil when there is no such sample or it is in already.

METHOD:: addBank
ARGUMENT:: bank
ARGUMENT:: max
Every sample of a bank, up to max (16).

METHOD:: removeAt
ARGUMENT:: i

METHOD:: move
ARGUMENT:: i
ARGUMENT:: to

METHOD:: clear

METHOD:: bpm
The tempo they play at; nil takes the first sample's own. See link::#-targetBpm::.

METHOD:: key
The key they play in, a link::Classes/String:: as link::Classes/SDGSampleTags#*parseKey:: reads
it: code::"Am"::, code::"F#"::, code::"Eb"::. nil takes the first melodic sample's key, as its
tempo leaves it. A string that is not a key is refused with a warning.

METHOD:: matchTempo
true: every loop with a bpm on the tempo's beats. false: each is stretched to its nearest whole cycles.

METHOD:: matchKey
true: every melodic sample into link::#-key::.

METHOD:: beatsPerCycle
4: a cycle is a bar of 4/4.

METHOD:: chopsPerBeat
How many pieces code::chop:: cuts a beat into; 0 is no chop.

METHOD:: useOffsets
Whether a loop whose first beat is late is shifted with code::<~::.

METHOD:: orbit
The orbit the preview plays into.

METHOD:: targetBpm
RETURNS:: link::#-bpm::, or the first sample's bpm, or 120.

METHOD:: cps
RETURNS:: the cycles a second the code sets.

METHOD:: targetKey
RETURNS:: code::(tonic:, mode:)::, or nil when the key is not matched or no sample is melodic.

METHOD:: plan
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Array:: of link::Classes/Event::s, one a sample: code::label::,
code::duration::, code::bpm::, code::beats::, code::cycles:: (loopAt's number), code::rate:: (the
tempo's read rate), code::tempoSt::, code::trim:: (the end of a loop cut to whole beats),
code::correction:: (semitones by speed), code::speed::, code::pitch:: (semitones in all),
code::chop::, code::shift:: (cycles earlier), code::keyFrom::, code::keyTo::, code::notes::.

METHOD:: code
RETURNS:: the Tidal code, a link::Classes/String::.

METHOD:: line
ARGUMENT:: r
one Event of link::#-plan::.
ARGUMENT:: d
the number after code::d::.
RETURNS:: one sample's line of code.

METHOD:: describe
ARGUMENT:: r
RETURNS:: the comment above a sample's line.

METHOD:: copy
Puts the code on the clipboard.
RETURNS:: whether this machine has a way to.

METHOD:: play
ARGUMENT:: orbitIndex
nil: link::#-orbit::.
Plays every sample here, in a loop, each piece as a code::\dirt:: event with the begin, end, speed,
code::unit "c":: and cps the code would give it, so it sounds as it would from Tidal.

METHOD:: stop

METHOD:: isPlaying

METHOD:: gui
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SDGSyncWindow::, opened or brought to the front.

METHOD:: window
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SDGSyncWindow:: once opened.

METHOD:: free
Stops the preview and closes the window.

METHOD:: tags
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SDGSampleTags:: of the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.

METHOD:: dirt
RETURNS:: the SuperDirt.
